cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use The Fly Hears, please cite this software using the metadata below.
  Please also cite the underlying datasets and relevant research listed in the
  README and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
type: software
title: The Fly Hears
authors:
  - family-names: Mavani
    given-names: Rahil
    website: https://github.com/rahilmavani
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/rahilmavani/fly-hears
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A local spoken-digit classification experiment that drives a frozen simulation
  of a selected fruit-fly connectome with audio features and trains a
  logistic-regression reader on its activity. Includes an interactive spike
  replay, a pretrained demo, and speaker-separated evaluation against scrambled
  wiring and audio-feature controls. Bundled data and model artifacts have
  separate licenses documented in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
keywords:
  - connectome
  - drosophila
  - reservoir computing
  - speech recognition
  - neuroscience
references:
  - type: data
    title: MaleCNS
    version: "1.0"
    authors:
      - name: FlyEM at HHMI Janelia Research Campus and collaborators
    url: https://male-cns.janelia.org/
    license: CC-BY-4.0
  - type: data
    title: Free Spoken Digit Dataset
    authors:
      - family-names: Jackson
        given-names: Zohar
      - name: FSDD contributors
